  "supported": [
    "All five nearby Adelie island populations share a dominant long-term decline component.",
    "The strength of the long-term shared component does not imply tight year-to-year synchrony; annual growth correlations are moderate and heterogeneous.",
    "Island identity accounts for substantial persistent variation in log abundance in addition to the shared year component.",
    "Litchfield is an extreme local endpoint, reaching zero breeding pairs from 2007 onward while the other four islands persist at low abundance through 2017.",
    "The data support a two-scale ecological framing: regional forcing sets the common direction while local island filters modulate annual response and extinction risk."
  ],
  "not_supported": [
    "a causal sea-ice effect from the year component alone",
    "a claim that island residuals are caused by competition",
    "uniform annual demographic synchrony across the five islands",
    "equivalent extinction risk across neighboring islands"
  ],
  "next_gate": "Freeze a mechanism model comparing regional sea-ice forcing with static island physical-habitat quality before opening those predictor values."
